# Who reviews what, by bounded context. GitHub asks the owners of every file a pull request
# changes to review it. For each pattern, the last line that matches wins.
#
# Each context owns its code and migrations, in apps/api/src/<context>/, its tests, in
# apps/api/test/<context>/, what it publishes, in packages/contracts/src/<context>/, and its
# dashboard screens. When a team takes on a context, put the team, such as
# @<organization>/<team>, in place of the owner on its lines. See ARCHITECTURE.md.

# The platform: everything no context owns, such as the composition root, the guards, the
# shared kernel, the dashboard's frame and the local stack.
